{"timestamp":1793350878980,"event":"userPromptSubmitted","sessionId":"f87abf3a-199d-4f2e-bda7-f7b996bdde15","agentId":null,"prompt":"Implement **Stage 1: Single-Approver Invoice Approval Limits** in the existing repository.\r\n\r\nFirst inspect `AGENTS.md`, the approval-domain skill, the existing domain model, API controllers, authentication/session handling, and unit tests.\r\n\r\n### Business requirements\r\n\r\n1. Manager can approve invoices up to and including 50,000.\r\n2. Director can approve invoices up to and including 500,000.\r\n3. Manager must not approve invoices above 50,000.\r\n4. Director must not single-approve invoices above 500,000 in this stage.\r\n5. Unauthorized approval attempts must return a clear error explaining the role limit.\r\n6. Rejected attempts must not mutate invoice status, decision fields, or repository state.\r\n7. Preserve existing submit and reject behavior.\r\n\r\n### Implementation constraints\r\n\r\n- Follow the existing architecture and coding conventions.\r\n- Pass the authenticated user's actual role from the API session to the domain approval service.\r\n- Enforce business rules in the domain layer, not only in the controller.\r\n- Do not hardcode a role for all users.\r\n- Do not implement the dual-approval feature yet. That belongs to Stage 2.\r\n- Update existing tests to match the new method signature.\r\n- Add positive, boundary, and negative unit tests, including unauthorized roles and unchanged state after rejection.\r\n- Inspect the generated tests and ensure they test behavior rather than implementation details.\r\n\r\n### Validation\r\nRun `dotnet test backend/InvoiceApp.sln`.\r\nFix any failures caused by your changes.\r\n\r\nDo not commit or push anything. At the end, summarize files changed, tests added, test results, and any unresolved issues."}
