{"timestamp":1793351328312,"event":"userPromptSubmitted","sessionId":"f87abf3a-199d-4f2e-bda7-f7b996bdde15","agentId":null,"prompt":"Implement Stage 2: Dual Approval for invoices above 500,000.\r\n\r\nRead AGENTS.md, the approval specification, task breakdown, and existing Stage 1 implementation first.\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n1. Invoices above 500,000 require two distinct approvers.\r\n2. The second approver must be a Director.\r\n3. The same username cannot approve twice.\r\n4. Invoice must remain PendingApproval after the first approval.\r\n5. After valid second approval, invoice becomes Approved.\r\n6. Invalid approval attempts must not mutate invoice or repository state.\r\n7. Preserve all Stage 1 Manager and Director approval limits.\r\n8. Store both approvers' usernames and approval timestamps.\r\n9. Return clear error messages for invalid attempts.\r\nImportant: Inspect the assignment requirements to determine who can provide the first approval for invoices above 500,000. If this is ambiguous, ask me before implementing rather than inventing a rule.\r\n\r\nAdd comprehensive positive and negative unit tests, including duplicate approver, non-Director second approver, and state preservation.\r\n\r\nRun `dotnet test backend/InvoiceApp.sln`, fix failures, and review your changes.\r\n\r\nDo not commit or push. Do not modify unrelated files.\r\n\r\nAt the end, summarize changed files, test results, and unresolved issues."}
