{"timestamp":1793512379675,"event":"userPromptSubmitted","sessionId":"f87abf3a-199d-4f2e-bda7-f7b996bdde15","agentId":null,"prompt":"Act as an independent senior code reviewer. Review the complete invoice approval implementation in this repository, including both Stage 1 and Stage 2.\r\n\r\nReview the changes against these requirements:\r\n\r\n1. Manager can approve invoices up to and including 50,000.\r\n2. Director can approve invoices up to and including 500,000.\r\n3. Invoices above 500,000 require two distinct Directors.\r\n4. First Director approval must leave the invoice PendingApproval.\r\n5. Second distinct Director approval must change the invoice to Approved.\r\n6. Same user cannot approve twice.\r\n7. Unauthorized and rejected attempts must not mutate invoice or repository state.\r\n8. Check concurrency handling and potential race conditions.\r\n9. Check API authorization and role validation.\r\n10. Check unit tests, negative test cases, and missing edge cases.\r\nAlso review code quality, security, maintainability, and error handling.\r\n\r\nRun:\r\n\r\n- `dotnet test backend/InvoiceApp.sln`\r\n- `git diff --check`\r\nDo not modify files, commit, or push anything.\r\n\r\nProduce a detailed review report. For EVERY finding include:\r\n\r\n- Finding ID\r\n- Severity: Critical / High / Medium / Low\r\n- File and line number\r\n- Description and impact\r\n- Recommended fix\r\n- Verdict: Fixed / Dismissed / Deferred\r\n- Reason for the verdict\r\nDo not invent findings. Clearly distinguish actual defects from suggestions. List all passed checks and remaining risks."}
